    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. but some people argue that even with discounts, it's just a way to gatekeep the city and favor people who can afford to live in areas where they don't need to drive as much. do you think the environmental benefits actually justify the social cost, or is it just a flawed idea from the start?",
