      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This is the core tension in the debate, pitting environmental necessity against social equity. While some argue the climate imperative is so urgent that short-term social friction is necessary for long-term gain, others contend that if the policy inherently disadvantages vulnerable populations, it is fundamentally unfair. The effectiveness often hinges on *how* the policy is structured; a well-designed system prioritizing equity and robust alternatives can better justify the environmental gain than a poorly implemented punitive system.",
